## Project Overview

This project applies **Natural Language Processing (NLP)** techniques to analyze the evolution of international diplomatic discourse. Using a corpus of **10,952 speeches** from the UN General Assembly (1946–2024), the analysis explores how global priorities have shifted from post-war security concerns to modern sustainability agendas.

### 🏆 Academic Context

Submitted as the **W11+1 Summative Assessment** for **DS202A: Data Science for Social Scientists** at the **London School of Economics (LSE)**.

